    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Hence, a sire marker effect is declared to be significant at the $ \\alpha $-level if $ F > F_{N,N(n-2),[1-\\alpha]} $. The power of this test is the probability that the test statistic $ F $ exceeds this critical value,",
